{
  "requirement": "For node reads, the SDK constructs a `Snapshot` from\nthe contents returned by `Domain::node_content` and their\n`NodeContents::fingerprint` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`, without another read.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Snapshot<T> {\n    pub content: T,\n    pub fingerprint: Fingerprint,\n}\n\nimpl<T> Snapshot<T> {\n    pub fn new(content: T, fingerprint: Fingerprint) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<T: Clone> Clone for Snapshot<T>;\nimpl<T: Debug> Debug for Snapshot<T>;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n\n1. **Snapshot built from `Domain::node_content` contents and their `NodeContents::fingerprint`.**\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` runs `read_snapshot` on empty and large multi-byte content. It asserts `snapshot.content.format()` equals the original and `snapshot.fingerprint == fp(original)`. It also asserts the recorded `Dependency::Node` carries the same fingerprint.\n   - `fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` asserts `read_snapshot(...).fingerprint == fp(\"before\")`. It also checks that a read after the content changes records a different fingerprint.\n   - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` asserts `snapshot.content.fingerprint() == snapshot.fingerprint` after the underlying content changed. It also asserts the fingerprint value is `before`.\n   - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` checks fingerprints from real domain contents.\n   - `fn[graph_tools_record_delivered_snapshots_and_prepared_pages_do_not_record_delivery]` and `fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` check the node-read dependency fingerprints, including `fp(\"subject\")` and `fp(\"implementation\")`.\n\n2. **No other read.**\n   - The read log is asserted exactly. In `fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` it is `[1,1,1,2]`: one read per call, and the failing read of node 2 still counts as one read.\n   - In `fn[direct_reads_return_complete_unicode_contents_and_snapshots]` it is `[1,1]`.\n   - In `fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` it is `[1]` after `read_snapshot` and the `fingerprint()` and `format()` calls.\n   - In `fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` it is `[1,3,2,3,1]`, one read per insertion.\n   - A fingerprint computed with an extra read, or from a later version, would fail these assertions.\n\n3. **The `Snapshot` shape and `Snapshot::new(content, fingerprint)`.**\n   - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[callers_can_pair_content_with_its_fingerprint]` constructs a snapshot with `new` and asserts both public fields.\n   - `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the export inventory, which lists `struct Snapshot` with `content`, `fingerprint` and `new()`.\n   - `#[non_exhaustive]` is a compile-time property, and the integration tests only use `Snapshot::new` from outside the crate.\n\n4. **`Clone` and `Debug` implementations.**\n   - I searched the implementation: `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph.rs#struct[Snapshot]` uses `#[derive(Clone, Debug)]`.\n   - Derived trait impls have no conditional and no transformation of their own, so they need no dedicated test.\n   - The `T: Clone` and `T: Debug` bounds are compile-time.\n\nThe cited `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint` is context only. Its fingerprint scheme and determinism are not assessed here.\n\nI found no adequacy gap, marking gap or acknowledgment issue.",
